<section>
  <h2>Worked example</h2>
  <p>
    Using the default <i>v</i>(<i>t</i>) = 3 + 2<i>t</i> − <i>t</i>², so
    <i>p</i> = 3, <i>q</i> = 2, <i>r</i> = −1:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li><i>a</i>(<i>t</i>) = 2 − 2<i>t</i></li>
    <li><i>s</i>(<i>t</i>) = 3<i>t</i> + <i>t</i>² − <i>t</i>³/3</li>
    <li>At <i>t</i> = 0: <i>v</i> = 3 m/s, <i>a</i> = 2 m/s², <i>s</i> = 0</li>
    <li>At <i>t</i> = 1 s: <i>v</i> = 4 m/s, <i>a</i> = 0, <i>s</i> = 3 + 1 − ⅓ = 3.67 m</li>
    <li>At <i>t</i> = 3 s: <i>v</i> = 0, <i>a</i> = −4 m/s², <i>s</i> = 9 m — instantaneously at rest</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    These match the live values if you Run and read the overlay at those
    times. Set <i>r</i> = 0 to recover constant acceleration
    <i>a</i> = <i>q</i>, with <i>s</i> = <i>p t</i> + ½<i>q t</i>².
  </p>
</section>
